  <text xml:lang="ta" type="edition">
    <body>

        <div xml:id="AN204.1-kilavi">
          <p type="edition">viṉaimuṟṟiya talaimakaṉ ṟērppākaṟkuc colliyatu.</p>
          <p type="translation" xml:lang="en">What HE whose work was finished said to [his] charioteer.</p>
        </div>
        <div rend="parallel">
      <lg xml:id="AN204.1">
        <l>ulakuṭa ṉiḻaṟṟiya tolaiyā veṇkuṭaik</l>
        <l>kaṭalpō ṟāṉaik kalimā vaḻuti</l>
        <l>vēttama ru[ḻa]nta viyaṉperum pācaṟaic</l>
        <l>ceṉṟuviṉai muṭittaṉa māyi ṉaṉṟē</l>
        <l>kārppeyark ketiriya kāṇṭaku puṟaviṟ</l>
        <l>kaṇaṅkoḷ vaṇṭi ṉañciṟait toḻuti</l>
        <l>maṇaṅkamaḻ mullai yā[r]ppa vutukkāṇ</l>
        <l>[van]taṉṟu vāḻi poḻutē valviraintu</l>
        <l>celka pākaniṉ ṉalviṉai neṭuntēr</l>
        <l>veṇṇe lariñar maṭivāyt taṇṇumai</l>
        <l>paṉmalarp poykaip paṭuppu ḷōppuṅ</l>
        <l>kāyneṟ paṭappai vāṇaṉ ciṟukuṭit</l>
        <l>taṇṭalai kamaḻuṅ kūnta</l>
        <l>loṇṭoṭi maṭantai tōḷiṇai peṟavē.</l>
      </lg>
      <lg type="translation" xml:lang="en">
        <l corresp="4">That day, when we have finished the work, going</l>
        <l corresp="3">from the wide huge encampment that has borne the royal war</l>
        <l corresp="2">of Vaḻuti  with spirited horses, an army like the sea,</l>
        <l corresp="1">[and] an unvanquished white umbrella that gives shade to all the world,</l>
        <l corresp="8a-c">the time has come – let it live –</l>
        <l corresp="6">when the pretty-winged multitude of bees in swarms</l>
        <l corresp="7">hums [around] the jasmine fragrant with scent, look there,</l>
        <l corresp="5">in the woodland fit to be seen, in the face of what has the name monsoon rains.</l>
        <l rend="indent6" corresp="8d">Very speedily</l>
        <l corresp="9">let go, o charioteer, the well-crafted chariot,</l>
        <l corresp="14">– [for me] to reach both shoulders of the girl with bright bangles</l>
        <l corresp="13">[and] tresses fragrant of the flower gardens</l>
        <l corresp="12">of the little hamlet of Vāṇaṉ, in gardens of unripe fruit [and] paddy,</l>
        <l corresp="10">where the leather-mouthed  Taṇṇumai drum of the cutters of white rice</l>
        <l corresp="11">scares away the birds descending onto ponds with many blossoms.</l>
      </lg>
        </div>
